ta, Georgia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/65143"} "93 from 22 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The United States was the heavy favorite in this race. They had won the last three Olympic gold medals, and the World Championships in 1993 and 1995. With no GDR to worry about by 1996, only Russia, second in both World Championships, was considered a challenger. But the final was much closer than expected. Russia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/75370"} "Yekaterina Leshchova"] " led on the opening leg. The 100 metre gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/77805"} "Gail Devers"] ", ran the second leg but could not get ahead of " [:a {:href "/athletes/64997"} "Chandra Sturrup"] " of the Bahamas. On the third leg, " [:a {:href "/athletes/77917"} "Inger Miller"] " pulled ahead and " [:a {:href "/athletes/77990"} "Gwen Torrence"] " anchored the US home to the gold medal. Miller was the daughter of Jamaican sprinter, " [:a {:href "/athletes/72310"} "Lennox Miller"] ", who had won Olympic medals in the 1968 and 1972 100 metres."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "42.49 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "41.95 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/77837"} "Chryste Gaines"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77805"} "Gail Devers"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77917"} "Inger Miller"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77990"} "Gwen Torrence"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77851"} "Carlette Guidry-White"]]] [:tr {:cla